# Backend Architecture (Node.js + Express)

## Layer Boundaries — NEVER Cross These

```
Routes      → Call controllers only. No business logic. No DB access.
Controllers → Call services only. Handle HTTP req/res. No business logic.
Services    → Call repositories only. Contain all business logic.
Repositories→ Call Mongoose models only. Contain all DB queries.
Models      → Define schema only. No business logic.
```

## Route File Template

```javascript
const express = require('express');
const router = express.Router();
const { authenticate, requireRole } = require('../../middleware/auth.middleware');
const { rateLimiter } = require('../../middleware/rateLimiter.middleware');
const { validate } = require('../../middleware/validate.middleware');
const [name]Controller = require('../../controllers/[name].controller');
const { [name]Validators } = require('../../validators/[name].validators');

router.use(rateLimiter);
// Routes here...
module.exports = router;
```

## Controller Template

```javascript
const asyncHandler = require('../utils/asyncHandler');
const [Name]Service = require('../services/[name].service');
const { successResponse, errorResponse } = require('../utils/response');

const methodName = asyncHandler(async (req, res) => {
  const result = await [Name]Service.methodName(req.user.id, req.body);
  return successResponse(res, 200, 'Success message', result);
});
```

## Service & Repository Templates

```javascript
// Service — business logic only, no HTTP, no direct DB
const methodName = async (userId, data) => {
  // Validate business rules, call repositories, return processed result
};

// Repository — ALL database queries, parameterized always
const findById = async (id) => {
  return await [Name]Model.findById(id).lean();
};
```

## API Response Format

```javascript
// Success
{ "success": true, "message": "Human readable message", "data": { ... } }

// Error
{ "success": false, "message": "Human readable error message", "errors": [ ... ] }

// Paginated
{ "success": true, "message": "...", "data": [ ... ], "pagination": { "page": 1, "limit": 20, "total": 450, "totalPages": 23 } }
```

## Audit Trail

Log every significant action:
```javascript
await AuditService.log({
  actorId: req.user.id,
  actorRole: req.user.role,
  action: 'ACTION_NAME',
  targetId: targetUser._id,
  targetType: 'User',
  ipAddress: req.ip,
  outcome: 'success'
});
```

Must log: registration/login, suspension/deletion, verification events, admin overrides, payments, disputes, consent changes, data exports, failed auth attempts.
